Hi there!
I tried to mess with it using events once. Mess witht he pattern of the event. I found it kind confusing... If your character is moving or does have step animation(which seems to me that it has, since you checked the walking and stepping box on the event page), the pattern will keep updating according to animation count. I think it's hard to debug something like that with events.
JavaScript:
Game_CharacterBase.prototype.updateAnimation = function() {
    this.updateAnimationCount();
    if (this._animationCount >= this.animationWait()) {
        this.updatePattern();
        this._animationCount = 0;
    }
};

Game_CharacterBase.prototype.animationWait = function() {
    return (9 - this.realMoveSpeed()) * 3;
};

Game_CharacterBase.prototype.updateAnimationCount = function() {
    if (this.isMoving() && this.hasWalkAnime()) {
        this._animationCount += 1.5;
    } else if (this.hasStepAnime() || !this.isOriginalPattern()) {
        this._animationCount++;
    }
};

Game_CharacterBase.prototype.updatePattern = function() {
    if (!this.hasStepAnime() && this._stopCount > 0) {
        this.resetPattern();
    } else {
        this._pattern = (this._pattern + 1) % this.maxPattern();
    }
};
So I guess is better if this is handled by a plugin:
Hakuen Studio Character Manager for RPG Maker MZ by Hakuen Studio
Change colors, scale, offset, and much more of the character sprites!
hakuenstudio.itch.io
You can have more control of the pattern order the character will follow and also if it will keep updating automatically or not update at all. Hope it helps
